      "description": "Watch Hull City vs Manchester United highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Hull City hosted the giants Manchester United in a highly anticipated Premier League clash. Fans gathered on this summer afternoon to witness a battle between tactical discipline and overwhelming possession. Hull's First-Half Blitz On August 22, 2026 , the match began with Manchester United looking to assert their dominance. However, it was Hull City who drew first blood in the 17th minute. Following a corner from Regan Slater , the ball fell kindly for Semi Ajayi , who reacted quickest to fire home with his right foot. The goal sent the home support into raptures and forced the visitors to rethink their strategy. Things went from good to better for the Tigers in the 38th minute. Nobel Mendy rose highest to head home another pinpoint delivery from Slater . A tense VAR check followed, causing a momentary hush across the stadium, but the goal was ultimately confirmed. Tensions flared shortly after as Matt Crooks was booked for dissent, reflecting the growing frustration within the United ranks. Resilient Defense Thwarts United's Comeback The second half saw Manchester United throw everything at the opposition. Managerial changes brought Marcus Rashford , Kobbie Mainoo , and Benjamin Sesko into the fray, resulting in a staggering 72% possession for the visitors. Despite the pressure, clear-cut chances were hard to come by. Ayden Heaven and Sesko saw headers blocked by a resolute Hull backline, with John Egan putting in a commanding performance. In the dying stages, Hull City remained focused. Liam Millar was cautioned for simulation as United's attacks became increasingly desperate. Harry Maguire missed a late opportunity, sending his effort wide of the target. When the final whistle blew, the home side celebrated a hard-fought victory, proving that clinical finishing and defensive organization can overcome even the most dominant spells of possession."
